  "goodToKnow": "Die Markthalle is a covered market hall. In the 19th century, cities like Berlin built Markthallen for hygiene reasons; some, like the Markthalle Neun in Kreuzberg, have been revived as food halls with street-food events. Stuttgart's Art Nouveau Markthalle opened in 1914. The outdoor equivalent is der Wochenmarkt. Plural: die Markthallen."
